{"type":"standard","title":"Elaine Luria","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Elaine Luria</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q58323073","titles":{"canonical":"Elaine_Luria","normalized":"Elaine Luria","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Elaine Luria</span></span>"},"pageid":58785816,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Rep._Elaine_Luria_official_photo%2C_117th_Congress.jpg/330px-Rep._Elaine_Luria_official_photo%2C_117th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":495},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/Rep._Elaine_Luria_official_photo%2C_117th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":683,"height":1024},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377442022","tid":"81da95ef-bbfa-11f1-8804-19ef1b7d672a","timestamp":"2026-09-29T11:40:02Z","description":"American politician (born 1975)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elaine_Luria","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elaine_Luria?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elaine_Luria?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Elaine_Luria"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elaine_Luria","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Elaine_Luria","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elaine_Luria?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Elaine_Luria"}},"extract":"Elaine Goodman Luria is an American politician and US Navy veteran who served as the U.S. representative from Virginia's 2nd congressional district from 2019 to 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, she is her party's nominee for the same seat in the 2026 election, a rematch against Republican incumbent Jen Kiggans, who defeated her in 2022.","extract_html":"<p><b>Elaine Goodman Luria</b> is an American politician and US Navy veteran who served as the U.S. representative from Virginia's 2nd congressional district from 2019 to 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, she is her party's nominee for the same seat in the 2026 election, a rematch against Republican incumbent Jen Kiggans, who defeated her in 2022.</p>"}